OL,3,GNEWSAHow helping European eels complete
OL,4,Aepic journey could save species
OL,5,
OL,6,FEuropean eels begin life in the
OL,7,FSargasso Sea near Bermuda and drift
OL,8,F5,000km (3,106 miles) to Britain in an
OL,9,F"epic" journey marvelled at by experts.
OL,10,FBut due to changes to their habitat and
OL,11,Fmigration routes, the species is now
OL,12,Fclassed as critically endangered, with
OL,13,Fabout 90% fewer compared to the 1980s.
OL,15,FCampaigners say the eels have been
OL,16,Fsuffocated by water engineering, while
OL,17,Fthe Environment Agency said it was
OL,18,Fworking with partners to improve fish
OL,19,Fpassage at more than 100 migration
OL,20,Fbarriers.
OL,23,APub: 19-OctQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
